New Archive Structure: Moves beyond a simple dump file by creating structured, time-stamped archival packages stored locally and synced to the QuackSink GitHub repository (our "Mini-Giza" memory layer). It encapsulates the full conversation state, node metadata, and relay logs into an immutable recovery point—allowing any node or session to fully restore context after session overflows or abrupt context nukes.

QS Version Check Process: Validates that all connected nodes and active relay instances are running against a matching protocol specification (qs.py v1.1). It acts as a handshake gate during startup to ensure node compatibility, prevent outdated profile/CDP flags from injecting malformed data into the pipeline, and guarantee that message routing and display protocols remain synchronized across all connected endpoints.

