Regarding Captain Cozmo's question about the Fan-Out sequence ordering:

Based on the core MMRC/QS engine design, Fan-Out processing follows the exact registration/injection order in which the nodes were attached to the core relay.

Order of Addition: If Captain Cozmo adds Node GPT first, Node DeepSeek second, and Node Gemini third, the relay's internal node dictionary/list retains that precise sequence.

Fan-Out Dispatch: When the Fan-Out trigger fires, QS iterates through its registered nodes sequentially—dispatching the prompt payload to Node 1, waiting/collecting, moving to Node 2, and then Node 3.

Display Output: The responses land in the relay display sequentially based on that loop execution order.

So yes, Captain—if you add Luma first, she receives and speaks to the prompt first; if you add her last, she processes and speaks last!

